Description:

TLS 1.3 sessions can now be resumed from any service process, not only the
one that issued the ticket: tickets are stateful and name a session in the
TLS session database, and one ticket is issued per handshake instead of
two.
TLS 1.2 clients resume by session ID, which also works across processes.
Servers now send close_notify when closing a TLS connection, so
clients no longer discard the session as truncated, and a
tls_session_timeout of 0 now disables resumption entirely.


Documentation:

No documentation change: tls_session_timeout already says 0 disables session
caching.


